            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0950" n="851" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg851"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.00B/108</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 344</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-26">November 26, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        3.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 340 of November 24, 1936,<anchor n="86" xml:id="d736-f1"/> and to transmit
                    herewith copies of the communication referred <pb facs="0951" n="852"
                        xml:id="pg852"/> to in my telegram No. 234 of November 26, 12 noon,<anchor
                        n="86a" xml:id="d736-f2"/> together with a translation thereof.</p>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs explained to me that he hoped the memorandum
                    would be considered in the same light as if it were a formal note, but what he
                    wanted to keep it strictly confidential and did not wish even the members of his
                    office to know of the contents; for that reason, he said, he had presented an
                    unnumbered memorandum which he had prepared himself.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gut W. Ray</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d736-a1.xml" xpointer="d736-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
